`ls --grants` (Dukovo's own, ADR 0443) shows who can reach each file
named instead of listing it: the accounts that may read or change it,
and which of the caller's apps would. reach(1) answers; ls hands it the
names, with `--` first, and gives back what it writes and its exit
status. Nothing changes without the flag.

